course: dictionary
lesson: 7942
title: Reasonable: fair, sensible, and not too much
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: «Reasonable» is a word you will meet in stories, in shops, and in maths. Its main meaning is fair and sensible. If someone is reasonable, they listen and do not demand too much.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «He grows at a reasonable pace» is about speed, so it means not too fast and not too slow. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
explain: In maths, a reasonable answer is one that makes sense. Before you trust an answer, estimate it. 49 × 21 is about 50 × 20, which is about 1000, so an answer of 10 is not reasonable.
fact: «Reasonable» means fair and sensible.
fact: A reasonable price is not too much and not too little.
fact: «Reasonable» can also mean fairly good, but not excellent.
fact: In maths, a reasonable answer is one that makes sense when you estimate it.
fact: The adverb is «reasonably», as in «reasonably cheap» or «reasonably well».
exercise: The Dormouse grows «at a reasonable pace». What does reasonable mean here? | Completely still | *Not too fast and not too slow | Backwards | Very fast and wild
exercise: Is 10 a reasonable answer for 49 × 21? | Yes, it is exactly right | Yes, because small numbers are always reasonable | Only if you use a calculator | *No, it is far too small, because 49 × 21 is about 1000
exercise: Find the word that fits: «Please just be ___ and listen to my side.» | glum | *reasonable | barely | ancient
test: Tom's drawing is reasonable, not perfect. What does reasonable mean here? | Very bad | Invisible | Perfect in every way | *Fairly good, but not excellent
test: Which request is reasonable? | Give me all your sweets right now | I want the whole park to myself | Everyone must do my homework for me | *Can I have a turn on the swing after you?
exam: Which sentence uses «reasonable» correctly? | The reasonable answer was 10,000 for 49 × 21. | The reasonable castle stood on the hill. | *A reasonable person listens to both sides before deciding. | She ran reasonable across the room.
